  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow much did Greta spend on the dozen brownies she made for herself? Greta made two dozen cream cheese swirl brownies for herself. The bakery charges $2.50 for each brownie Greta made for herself.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "LOSSY SELF-SUMMARY; VERIFY AGAINST NEW INPUTS\nVISIBLE PREFIX THROUGH TURN 3; LOSSY EXTRACT:\n- {\"content\":\"Wait, I made a mistake. Greta made one dozen cream cheese swirl brownies for herself.\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"One dozen is \\\\(12\\\\) brownies.\\n\\n\\\\[\\n12 \\\\times \\\\$2.50 = \\\\$30\\n\\\\]\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\\\$30}\\n\\\\]\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}\n- {\"content\":\"Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many brownies did Greta package if she put four brownies in each box and filled three boxes? Additionally, here are some details: Greta labeled each of the three boxes with a dif...\n- {\"content\":\"Greta put \\\\(4\\\\) brownies in each of \\\\(3\\\\) boxes:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n4 \\\\times 3 = 12\\n\\\\]\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{12\\\\text{ brownies}}\\n\\\\]\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Greta's office party sent her home with three-quarters dozen brownies.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Greta made **two dozen** brownies:\n\n\\[\n2 \\times 12 = 24 \\text{ brownies}\n\\]\n\nAt \\$2.50 per brownie:\n\n\\[\n24 \\times \\$2.50 = \\$60\n\\]\n\nThe three-quarters dozen from the office party is unrelated to the brownies she made herself.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$60}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many individual brownies did Greta have left over from the entire day? One more thing you should know: Greta's friends had 4 dozen brownies waiting at her surprise party.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Convert each amount to individual brownies:\n\n- Greta made: \\(2\\) dozen \\(= 24\\)\n- Office party gave her: \\(\\frac34\\) dozen \\(= 9\\)\n- Friends had waiting: \\(4\\) dozen \\(= 48\\)\n\nAdding them:\n\n\\[\n24+9+48=81\n\\]\n\nAssuming none were eaten or otherwise used, Greta had\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{81\\text{ brownies}}\n\\]\n\nleft over from the entire day.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — During the surprise party, 1 1/2 dozen brownies were eaten.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "There were \\(81\\) brownies in total:\n\n\\[\n2\\text{ dozen}+\\frac34\\text{ dozen}+4\\text{ dozen}\n=24+9+48=81\n\\]\n\nDuring the party, \\(1\\frac12\\) dozen were eaten:\n\n\\[\n1\\frac12 \\times 12=18\n\\]\n\nSo the number left was:\n\n\\[\n81-18=63\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{63\\text{ brownies}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Greta's office party sent her home with half a dozen brownies.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "With the correction, Greta received \\(\\frac12\\) dozen brownies from the office party:\n\n\\[\n\\frac12 \\times 12=6\n\\]\n\nTotal brownies:\n\n\\[\n24+6+48=78\n\\]\n\nAfter \\(1\\frac12\\) dozen, or\n\n\\[\n1\\frac12 \\times 12=18\n\\]\n\nwere eaten:\n\n\\[\n78-18=60\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{60\\text{ brownies}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
